 challenging times  for pursuing that Target  and to be frank  I would acknowledge that recent Market  developments have created their own  additional challenges for the pursuit of  our Target  but despite these challenges  Mai and the NPC's commitment to  achieving two percent Target is  unwavering  foreign  now in the spirit of what we heard from  the vice president  we're broadly speaking use this using  the same framework we're employing  monetary policy to steer aggregate  demand around aggregate supply in a way  that relieves current inflationary  pressures in order to achieve our goal  the relevance of Market developments  comes from how they influence precisely  this process  but they have to be seen in the context  of other important macroeconomic  macroeconomic influences  including the fiscal news that was  announced last week  as well as developments in Energy prices  developments in labor markets and other  spaces that I think the vice president  has mentioned and I'm sure we'll talk  about later  the vehicle for making that necessarily  comprehensive assessment  is the NPC's forecast process which is  embodied in the round that we're now  beginning to start on leading up so the  mpc's decision meeting in early November  now given we also want to hear from  other members of the panel and have a  lively discussion I'll leave elements of  what's really going to enter into that  assessment for the discussion and for  the forecast itself although I do want  to flag clearly at this point that in my  view  the combination of fiscal announcement  we've seen will act as a stimulus to  demand in the economy  now I recognize for many of you in this  room  talking about November seems a long time  away  so I used to work as has been said in  financial markets and you know for those  of you doing algorithmic Trading a long  time can be nanoseconds  and even for those of you who are in the  media or political circles  you're operating a daily cycle or hourly  cycle 